easingly stiff.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn7le02ob04re2img05.jpg"}, {"time": "23000", "text": "To fight the disease, Cousins decided to add a twist to traditional medical treatment. He took a lot of Vitamin C and exposed himself to a steady diet of humor. He soon found that ten minutes of energetic laughter and a dose of Vitamin C allowed him two hours of painless sleep, and the inflammation in his joints had decreased. Cousins was convinced that \"laughter therapy\" was the key to his recovery.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn7le02ob04re2img05.jpg"}, {"time": "53000", "text": "Norman Cousins lived until the year 1990. By that time, he had become famous not only as a magazine editor but also as the discoverer of a new form of medical treatment. His book <span class=\"italic\">Anatomy of an Illness</span> persuaded many physicians to begin taking humor seriously as one means of improving their patients' health. Now that's something to tweet about!", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le02ob04re2img05.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le02ob04re2img05.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": [], "title": ""}], "id": 0}]}